# React Performance Standards

## Rendering
- Avoid inline object/array props when causing churn.
- Use `React.memo` only when profiling shows benefit.
- Prefer derived state over duplicated state.

## Lists
- Use stable keys; never use array index as key for dynamic lists.
- Virtualize long lists when needed.

## Code Splitting
- Lazy load large routes or heavy components.
- Avoid eager loading of rarely used code paths.
